# Environment Variables Configuration

This project uses Google Generative AI for wellness plan generation.

## Local Development Setup

1. Create a `.env.local` file in the root directory (Git-ignored automatically)
2. Add your Google Generative AI API key:

```
GOOGLE_GENAI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```

## Production Deployment (Vercel)

1. Go to your Vercel project settings
2. Navigate to **Environment Variables**
3. Add the following variable for all environments (Production, Preview, Development):

**Name:** `GOOGLE_GENAI_API_KEY`
**Value:** Your Google Generative AI API key

## Getting Your API Key

1. Visit [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikeys)
2. Click "Create API Key"
3. Copy the generated key
4. Add it to `.env.local` (local) and Vercel (production)

## Security Notes

- ✅ `.env.local` is git-ignored and never committed
- ✅ API keys are only read from environment variables
- ✅ Never hardcode API keys in your source code
- 🔄 Rotate API keys if they are ever exposed

## Testing

After setting up your API key:

1. Run locally: `npm run dev`
2. Test the wellness plan generation form
3. Verify Vercel deployment with the correct environment variable set
